   "Parse *s* into ISO ``YYYY-MM-DD``.\n\n    Returns a tuple ``(norm, ambiguous)``:\n      * ``norm``      — \"YYYY-MM-DD\" on success, else None.\n      * ``ambiguous`` — True when the value is a numeric date whose day & month\n                       are both ≤ 12 (so MM/DD and DD/MM are both valid) AND we\n                       had NO explicit format hint / dayfirst preference to break\n                       the tie.  Callers must keep the RAW value and warn the user\n                       rather than silently guessing.\n\n    Priority:\n      1. ``date_format`` (if given) — exact strptime, never ambiguous.\n      2. explicit unambiguous formats (ISO, text-month) — never ambiguous.\n      3. numeric formats — if only one parses (e.g. 13.03 → DD/MM only) it is\n         safe; if both parse, resolve by ``dayfirst`` but mark ambiguous unless\n         ``dayfirst`` was an explicit preference.\n    ",
   "",
   [
    null,
    false
   ],
   "%Y-%m-%d",
   false,
   1,
   0,
   true
  ],
